WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:00.913
- Hi, I'm Jen.

00:00:00.913 --> 00:00:01.746
- And I'm Niki.

00:00:02.151 --> 00:00:03.070
And today we're talking
about the untold stories

00:00:03.070 --> 00:00:04.833
of queer people throughout history.

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:05.763
- Ooh.

00:00:05.934 --> 00:00:06.767
- Ooh.

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:10.620
We're gonna look into
some rumors and stories

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:13.440
that are already there, they're
already floating around.

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:15.130
- Outing is still not okay, folks,

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:17.000
but these people are long
dead and we are doing

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.000
nobody's life any harm
by talking about them.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.400
In fact, we're probably
making your life better.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:28.940
- Today, we're talking about
the highly sought after,

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:31.070
very, very popular founding father

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:32.360
Alexander Hamilton.

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:34.650
- Oh, Alexander Hammy-ham-ham.

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:37.780
- As popularized by Lin-Manuel Miranda.

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:39.723
- In his play, Rent.

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:42.060
- Alexander Hamilton, rumored to have had

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:44.260
intimate relationships with
men outside of his marriage

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:45.500
to Eliza Schuyler.

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:46.333
- Interesting.

00:00:46.333 --> 00:00:47.613
Question, was he president?

00:00:48.017 --> 00:00:48.850
- No.

00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:49.683
What do you know about him,

00:00:49.683 --> 00:00:50.870
other than he was not president?

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:52.970
- I honestly don't know enough, so hit me.

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:57.290
Alexander Hamilton was
born January 11th, 1757

00:00:57.290 --> 00:01:00.090
in the British West Indies
to a father who abandoned him

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:02.150
and a mother who died when he was 11.

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:03.103
Not a great start.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.000
But he was very smart.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:06.730
So his friends and family were like,

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:08.180
wow, this kid's really smart,

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:10.000
we gotta do something about it.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.380
So they send him to a
prep school in New Jersey

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:14.530
and then later he gets to go
to King's College in New York,

00:01:14.530 --> 00:01:16.920
which is actually now Columbia.

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:17.753
Ivy League.

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:19.620
And then, bam, it's pretty
much the Revolutionary War.

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:21.680
Around this time, he
marries Elizabeth Schuyler.

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:22.870
- [Jen] Oh beautiful.

00:01:22.870 --> 00:01:26.933
- [Niki] Socialite, she's hot,
she's cute, and she's rich.

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:28.463
- Oh, she's just like me.

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:29.590
Hot and rich.

00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:31.130
- While he's in school in New York,

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:34.040
revolts against Great Britain start,

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:35.660
and he becomes an influential voice

00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:36.860
in speaking out for the rebellion.

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:40.270
Cut to February 1777,
George Washington invites

00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:42.570
Alexander Hamilton to be his aide-de-camp,

00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:45.260
which is like a secretary
administrative role

00:01:45.260 --> 00:01:46.093
in the military.

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:47.980
And then guess who else
is also an aide-de-camp

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:48.813
around this time?

00:01:48.813 --> 00:01:49.863
John Laurens.

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:52.750
John Laurens born in 1754 has
a very different upbringing

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:53.623
than Hamilton.

00:01:53.870 --> 00:01:56.210
Grows up rich, gets sent
to a fancy prep school

00:01:56.210 --> 00:01:58.313
in Switzerland, but how romantic?

00:01:58.660 --> 00:01:59.850
He's got everything growing up.

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:01.070
Hamilton's got nothing growing up.

00:02:01.070 --> 00:02:02.860
It's like the beginning of a movie.

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:05.360
Some people believe that
Hamilton and Laurens

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:07.610
shared more than a close friendship.

00:02:07.610 --> 00:02:09.380
Another biographer named Ron

00:02:09.710 --> 00:02:10.543
whose biography.

00:02:10.543 --> 00:02:11.423
- Named Ron.

00:02:11.910 --> 00:02:14.280
- He says at the very least,

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:16.790
we can say that Hamilton
developed something like an

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:19.573
adolescent crush on his
friend John Laurens,

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:21.120
at the very least.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:23.203
- We're going more than
just the very least.

00:02:23.203 --> 00:02:24.036
- We're gonna go a
little further than that.

00:02:24.036 --> 00:02:24.980
- We're going to the most.

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:27.490
- Also, it's fishy because Hamilton's son,

00:02:27.490 --> 00:02:29.680
who was responsible for
his father's biography,

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:32.160
purposefully leaves things out

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:33.980
about Hamilton and Laurens.

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:35.450
- To me, it sort of speaks to

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:37.813
trying to preserve this
image of his father.

00:02:37.910 --> 00:02:39.180
The basis of these rumors

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:41.310
is in the letters that
Hamilton and Laurens exchanged.

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:43.270
We need to know that this is wartime.

00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:44.663
Emotions are high.

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:45.743
Here we go.

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:48.780
Cold in my professions,
warm in my friendships,

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:50.310
I wish my dear Laurens,

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:53.640
it might be in my power, by
action rather than words,

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:55.840
to convince you that I love you.

00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:58.650
I shall only tell you that
'till you bade us adieu,

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:00.963
I hardly knew the value you had taught,

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:03.070
my heart to set upon you.

00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:05.443
- Don't make eye contact
with me when you read that.

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:06.940
- I'm gonna skip ahead of it

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:07.840
because he talks a lot.

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:10.010
But he goes on to say, you
should not have taken advantage

00:03:10.010 --> 00:03:12.330
of my sensibility to
steal into my affections

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:13.480
without my consent.

00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:15.990
But as you have done it and
as we are generally indulgent

00:03:15.990 --> 00:03:17.550
to those we love, I shall not scruple

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:19.170
to pardon the fraud you have committed

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:20.740
on condition that for my sake,

00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:22.103
if not for your own,

00:03:22.230 --> 00:03:25.170
you will always continue
to merit the partiality

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:27.773
which you have so artfully
instilled into me.

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:31.400
But immediately you feel
yawny and uncomfortable.

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:34.450
- Yeah, I am trying to
squeeze it up into myself

00:03:35.830 --> 00:03:38.450
'cause that is somebody who is in love.

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:40.033
- This is my translation.

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:43.750
Hey, dude, I wish I could
show you how much I love you,

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:45.060
not just write you letters.

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:47.110
Look at how you made me like you so much.

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:49.560
I'll forgive you for seducing me because

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:50.520
I kinda like it a lot.

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:53.340
This letter is pretty
odd on multiple accounts

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:55.640
because later, Hamilton then asks Laurens

00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:58.333
to help him find a wife
while he's in South Carolina.

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:01.393
To excite their, their being the honeys,

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:04.570
emulation, it will be
necessary for you Laurens

00:04:04.570 --> 00:04:08.653
to give an account of the
lover, his size, make,

00:04:08.710 --> 00:04:11.343
quality of mind, and body,

00:04:11.530 --> 00:04:14.213
achievements, expectations,
fortune, et cetera.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:16.240
In drawing my picture,

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:18.740
you will no doubt be civil to your friend.

00:04:18.740 --> 00:04:21.590
Mind you, do justice to
the length of my nose

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:23.447
and don't forget that I (bleep).

00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:26.470
The letter is scratched out after that.

00:04:26.470 --> 00:04:30.180
So people believe that he
was talking about his dingy

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:33.450
'cause literally he's
like, oh, you have to go

00:04:33.450 --> 00:04:35.670
talk me up to the ladies
and find me a wife.

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:38.430
Don't forget to tell them about my body

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:40.093
and the length of my nose.

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:44.670
- The fact that there is
some sexual undertones

00:04:44.670 --> 00:04:46.680
makes me think that there was at least

00:04:46.854 --> 00:04:48.453
a hand job.

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:51.120
- And in other letters to Laurens,

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:53.350
Hamilton refers to himself and his actions

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:55.393
as those of a jealous lover.

00:04:55.430 --> 00:04:57.490
I have still a part for the public

00:04:57.550 --> 00:04:58.823
and another for you.

00:04:59.390 --> 00:05:02.690
So if you're impatience to
have me married is misplaced,

00:05:02.690 --> 00:05:04.363
a strange cure by the way,

00:05:04.390 --> 00:05:05.970
as if after matrimony

00:05:05.970 --> 00:05:08.400
I was to be less devoted than I am now.

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:09.800
Let me tell you

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:12.940
that I intend to restore
the empire of Hymen

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:15.673
and that Cupid is to
be his prime minister.

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:18.490
I wish you were at liberty
to transgress the bounds

00:05:18.490 --> 00:05:19.523
of Pennsylvania.

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:21.640
I would invite you after the fall

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:24.663
to Albany to witness
the final consummation.

00:05:25.230 --> 00:05:27.593
- They were fooking.

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:29.590
Seriously, that to me,

00:05:29.590 --> 00:05:33.700
this letter is to me the clearest sign

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:35.070
because Hamilton's basically saying,

00:05:35.070 --> 00:05:36.280
you want me to get married

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:38.090
because you think we're going
to be stop being in love

00:05:38.090 --> 00:05:40.830
once I'm married but you're wrong as hell.

00:05:40.830 --> 00:05:43.330
Not language you use to
someone you're speaking to

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:44.520
strictly platonically.

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:46.010
- So we have a lot of
letters from Hamilton,

00:05:46.010 --> 00:05:49.240
fewer from Laurens, but the
ones we do have access to,

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:51.330
he writes to Hamilton,
shortly before he dies.

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:52.180
Oh, do you want to read this?

00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:53.130
You can be Laurens.

00:05:53.130 --> 00:05:54.350
- Adieu, my dear friend,

00:05:54.350 --> 00:05:57.310
while circumstances place so
great a distance between us,

00:05:57.310 --> 00:05:58.370
I entreat you not

00:05:58.390 --> 00:06:00.623
to withdraw the consolation
of your letters.

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:02.690
You know the unalterable sentiments

00:06:02.690 --> 00:06:04.170
of your affectionate Laurens.

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:05.620
- Less flowery language

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:07.430
but still clear in intention.

00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:09.843
Don't stop sexting me
because I kinda like it.

00:06:11.107 --> 00:06:12.840
John Laurens unfortunately dies.

00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:15.200
He was one of the last casualties
of the Revolutionary War.

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:16.370
So back to the biographers.

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:18.320
He also says that after Laurens died,

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:20.870
Hamilton never found a
close friend like him again.

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:25.670
There's just like a part of him.

00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:26.503
- That died with Laurens.

00:06:26.503 --> 00:06:27.830
- That was never the same, yeah.

00:06:27.830 --> 00:06:29.110
- What happens to Alexander?

00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:31.530
- So the Revolutionary War ends.

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:35.543
Hamilton helps draft up what
Congress is gonna look like,

00:06:35.590 --> 00:06:39.420
he studies law, helps write
most of the Federalist Papers.

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:41.840
Hamilton dies in a duel with Aaron Burr.

00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:44.430
- Just to clarify, duel
is when you turn around,

00:06:44.430 --> 00:06:45.913
you both shoot each other.

00:06:46.280 --> 00:06:47.113
So stupid.

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:48.680
- It was a different time.

00:06:48.890 --> 00:06:51.890
People were just really fast
and loose with duels and words.

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:53.970
- Interesting and fascinating

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:57.113
that there was perhaps a young
love between these two men.

00:06:57.320 --> 00:06:58.610
- It sounds like a great movie.

00:06:58.610 --> 00:07:00.013
So I hope you guys had fun

00:07:00.013 --> 00:07:02.010
and learned a little
bit of something today

00:07:02.010 --> 00:07:03.960
about our founding father
Alexander Hamilton.

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:05.270
We'll never know for sure,

00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:07.470
but at the very least, we can speculate

00:07:07.470 --> 00:07:11.040
and wildly assert that
they were for sure in love,

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:13.293
married, and will never forget each other.

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:14.363
- Yeah.

00:07:14.878 --> 00:07:16.140
If there's someone that
you suspect is queer

00:07:16.140 --> 00:07:17.920
throughout history, let us know.

00:07:17.920 --> 00:07:19.420
Maybe we'll talk about it.

00:07:19.420 --> 00:07:20.253
- Bye everybody.

00:07:20.253 --> 00:07:21.086
See you next time.

